WEBVTT

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:08.480
M-My lord!

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.530
Those bastards!

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.990
Those poisonous bugs devouring 
His Imperial Majesty's sacred garden!

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.000
Oscar!

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.130
Gather all our troops at once,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.630
and march on Findolf!

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.890
I-I thought you had entrusted that to 
Marquis Arclide and Marquis Buchwald?!

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:44.280
Then you can tell those incompetents this:

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.900
"If you don't want to be slain 
along with those pests,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.900
then cross the Ruruck Mountains 
at once and put them down!"

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.410
Th-The governor of the northern lands
has ordered all units to assemble at once!

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:07.420
So Gustave is gathering forces 
over 10,000 strong around himself.

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:08.620
Yes.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:12.300
Now that the Seven-Light Faith 
has defeated L'age Soleil,

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.730
we have a perfect opportunity to strike.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:41.370
<b>High School Prodigies Have It Easy
Even In Another World!</b>

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.860
<b>It Seems Tsukasa Has
Seen Through Everything!</b>

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.120
Cross the Ruruck Mountains in winter?!

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.260
He's sending us off to our deaths!

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.090
Why do we have to go through this?

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:07.980
I can't believe he would be this impatient.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.920
M-Marquis Arclide, you mustn't say such things.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.580
Thank you for the admonition, Marquis Buchwald.

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.380
But I had hoped we could wait until spring
and have a proper battle.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.040
Oslo El Gustave...

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.070
He may be an unparalleled warrior, 
but he's an awful leader.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:32.560
The Emperor chose the 
wrong man to grant rank.

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:36.490
Who are these Seven-Light Faith people anyway?

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:38.880
They're certainly a mysterious group.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.110
I just hope our 3,000 troops 
are enough to handle them.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.620
What?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.460
Let's have our forces rest
 at the Ruruck Checkpoint for now.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.380
All troops, open fire!

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.760
Wh-What?!

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.930
Gunshots?

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:06.010
It can't be...

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.510
All units retreat!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.330
Retreat?!

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:15.710
The Ruruck Checkpoint's already 
fallen into enemy hands.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.020
We'll be dead if we don't run.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.530
How many guns do those men have?

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.900
Unsurprisingly, Marquis Arclide 
was quick to act.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.120
All right!

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.020
Now, let's begin the pursuit!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.170
We're storming straight into Buchwald!

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:39.960
Lord Arclide!

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.740
Our rear guard is being obliterated
 by the enemy's pursuing forces!

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.560
At this rate...

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.450
Tell all the units that Arclide died
in the enemy attack.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.020
But if we do that, our army
will collapse into a rout!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.410
Let them.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:57.520
That will make those 
pursuing us feel satisfied.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.510
Right now, they're getting greedy.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:02.880
They're hoping to reduce our numbers,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.030
even if it means abandoning their 
advantageous position at the checkpoint.

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.310
I see!

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:11.540
We'll fake a rout and lure them
into the open fields.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:15.200
You go on ahead, meet up with
the squads in the second wave,

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.320
and get them into formation for a charge!

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.350
Yes, sir! Leave it to me!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.420
Heavy cavalry!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.840
Cavalry, charge!

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:17.500
Guns won't stop them.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.750
That's heavy cavalry for you!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.910
I'd like to ask you to drive off
 the punitive force.

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:31.870
If our enemy is smart,

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.200
they'll recognize their disadvantage at 
the checkpoint and in the mountains,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.800
and they'll make a strategic retreat.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.790
In which case,

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.670
they'll probably send their 
precious heavy cavalry in.

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.230
The moment their heavy cavalry charge in

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.050
and they've grown certain of victory,

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.440
make a point and crush them...

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.340
using these.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:01.370
Everything's going as Tsukasa predicted.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.300
What in the world?

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:11.850
Retreat.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.230
Everyone, fall back to Buchwald!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:21.920
We're setting off to slay
 those rebels infesting Findolf!

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:28.380
My army will not leave even 
a single ant in our wake!

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:33.180
We will paint the northern mountains red
with the rebels' blood!

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.940
The weight of our enemies' corpses 
is the weight of our loyalty!

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:42.750
We'll burn every last one 
of these foolish rebels

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.930
who dare oppose His Imperial Majesty 
until none remain!

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:54.570
What do you think you're doing?

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:59.310
Now is the time to rise up!

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.680
Azure Brigade!

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.830
Strike this traitorous vassal down!

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:21.480
<i>Ringo, Ringo!</i>

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:25.990
<i>It looks like Arclide and Buchwald 
are holing up in their castle, bear.</i>

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.400
Just as Tsukasa predicted.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.610
<i>Bear?</i>

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.900
Wh-What?!

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.720
What is going on?

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.840
<i>This is an announcement 
for everyone in Buchwald.</i>

00:09:09.840 --> 00:09:12.620
<i>As you can see, hiding behind castle walls</i>

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.280
<i>is useless against the Seven-Light Faith, bear.</i>

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:20.530
<i>We demand that you lay down your arms
in unconditional surrender, bear.</i>

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.040
<i>We hope you will make
the right decision, bear.</i>

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.020
M-Marquis Arclide...

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.230
We can't win.

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:40.300
<i>Mission accomplished, bear!</i>

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.680
<i>I wonder how Shinobu's 
doing on her end, bear.</i>

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.350
Yeah...

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.580
Duke Gustave!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.080
Our Azure Brigade has you surrounded!

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:14.300
The foundation of a nation is its people!

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.090
Without the people, there is no nation!

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:20.650
If you have any shred of reason
 left within you,

00:10:20.650 --> 00:10:23.280
then you will surrender 
with shame for your actions

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.430
and correct your ways as a vassal!

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:31.770
Without the people, 
there is no nation, you say?

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:36.030
Silence yourself, you fool!

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.560
A nation and the people

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:44.450
exist only to serve His Imperial Majesty!

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.500
The delusions of you lowly cur,

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.330
and your hubris...

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:53.090
I shall burn it all to the ground!

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.860
Sounds like he has no 
intention of surrendering.

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.430
Then we must do what needs done!

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:00.220
Let's go, Shinobu!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.970
Roger that!

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:33.710
Jeanne!

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:37.380
I'm all right!

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:42.090
Honestly, mages are such trouble.

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:43.720
Jeanne!

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.020
Fools!

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:13.500
My eyes!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.310
Traitor Gustave,

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:17.500
your head is mine!

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.510
You would call me

00:12:22.830 --> 00:12:24.760
a traitor?!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:30.470
How dare you?!

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:37.270
Seriously?

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.430
This ends now.

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:57.210
Why you!

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:14.600
Did we get him?

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.850
Ah, don't go saying that.

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:20.320
You bastards!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.880
You worms, defying the Emperor!

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.100
You and your insolent tricks!

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:44.900
This is not enough to defeat
 the great Gustave!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.630
Okay, this looks like seriously bad news.

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:49.090
Jeanne, over here!

00:13:57.200 --> 00:14:00.300
I can't believe he'd blow up 
the tower with himself inside.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.200
What a man...

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:07.840
In that old man's eyes,
everyone's lives, including his own,

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:10.540
existed solely to be offered up to the empire.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.130
So, how's the city doing?

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:28.150
Right, well, there's not much chaos.

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:31.420
Looks like your immediate and thorough
 relief efforts were effective.

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:33.660
Good to hear.

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:35.160
What happened with Gustave?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:39.270
Thing is, we never found a body.

00:14:40.070 --> 00:14:41.520
What do you think?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:46.490
Hmm, it's hard to believe that 
old man would kill himself.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:51.160
Though the members of the Azure Brigade 
are trying to pronounce him dead.

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:58.290
They're going around boasting that the Azure
Brigade has slain the traitorous Gustave.

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.200
Well, I'm sure they do.

00:15:00.200 --> 00:15:02.080
I think that does it for my report.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.640
Well, I'll be heading off now.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:06.800
Yeah, go have some fun.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.190
Oh, right, right.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:10.300
How are the lords on your end doing?

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:11.940
No problems there.

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:14.780
He's doing good work for us.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:22.970
A-Are you really pledging allegiance 
to them, Marquis Arclide?

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:25.000
There's no other option.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:29.070
These guns are equipped with rifling

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:31.540
that even the Imperial Workshop 
has failed to implement.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.400
Then there's also this magical 
Haber-Bosch Process, used to produce

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.200
an infinite amount of gunpowder from the air.

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:40.830
This goes way beyond a mere
difference in technological level.

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.460
Not only that,

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:47.590
but all of the strategies and decisions 
I made in Ruruck are written in here.

00:15:47.590 --> 00:15:52.340
These are documents penned by Tsukasa, 
an angel of the Seven-Light Faith.

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:58.400
So he had seen through all of my thoughts 
before the battle had even begun.

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:02.100
No way! Only a god could possibly...

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.000
Yes.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:06.410
And no human can best a god.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:13.300
I, Arclide, will humbly join 
the banner of the Seven-Light Faith.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.380
This feels so good.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:34.880
It's like we're lying in a field of flowers.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:38.480
Incredible.

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.390
Lyrule's totally into it, too.

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:47.270
I heard these were super luxurious 
aroma oils used by the Empress.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.780
I-I shouldn't be using something so special!

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.310
It's fine, it's fine.

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.530
Everything is a learning experience, Lyrule.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:59.320
You've been studying magic lately
with old man Gale, right?

00:16:59.320 --> 00:17:00.900
Y-Yes.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:04.190
Apparently, these oils are 
created by imperial mages

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:08.040
using the power of spirits to 
extract their active ingredient.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.050
Mages made these?

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.870
That's right.

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.520
There's great magic like this out there!

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:19.660
And you've had a rough few days, Ringo.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:21.770
You should take this chance to relax...

00:17:22.470 --> 00:17:24.440
What's up, Ringo?

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.710
I'm, um...

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:36.380
not as pretty as all of you are,

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:42.740
and I don't have...

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:47.350
a great figure, either...

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:51.000
What are you saying?

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:57.760
You're a top contender in the cuteness
category with these smooth cheeks!

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.210
That's right.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:04.770
There are many men who would love to 
protect a lady as cute as you, Ringo-san.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.870
My body's so ripped with muscles

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:11.270
that it makes me jealous of 
how soft you are sometimes.

00:18:11.270 --> 00:18:15.640
I think you're lovely and cute too, Ringo.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:16.790
Very!

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:22.540
As for your figure, that just 
depends on your efforts.

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:26.320
Would you like to try out the big breast
massages passed down my family?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:30.250
Oh, you have a technique for that?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.170
It's effective on men, after all.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.260
It was necessary for kunoichi.

00:18:41.990 --> 00:18:43.510
<i>I don't want to lose!</i>

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.180
Please do it!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.420
Nin, nin!

00:18:47.880 --> 00:18:51.900
It might tickle at first, though.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.400
You start here and do this...

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.410
and then you do this here.

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:01.050
No!

00:19:01.410 --> 00:19:04.760
You're so cute, Ringo-chan.

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:08.410
Then you do this

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.500
and this...

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.260
Why do I have to endure this?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:15.940
Oh, my!

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:19.380
You're so sensitive, Akatsuki.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.550
Your skin's so pale, it's almost transparent,

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:23.720
and so juicy that my fingers sink right in...

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:28.800
Many men would greatly 
enjoy such wonderful skin.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.850
Stop it!

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.640
Wow, these are good leaves.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.610
Yeah. I hear they're expensive tea leaves
meant for the imperial family.

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:44.300
The women are enjoying their aroma massage, too.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:48.240
They're giving us every luxury 
afforded by this world's standards.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:52.400
Micchan, Makkun, sorry for the wait!

00:19:52.400 --> 00:19:55.250
Oh, the goddesses have appeared!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.040
Wha?!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:00.490
Hey, hey, who's that blonde, 
short-haired beauty with you?

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:01.930
I'll punch you!

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.930
You're looking pretty cute, man.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.680
This is your fault!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:09.150
You're one thing, Masato,

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:12.080
but how could you be so cruel as 
to abandon me like that, Tsukasa?!

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.140
Sorry.

00:20:13.140 --> 00:20:17.950
But I had no other choice but to allow it
in order to secure your safety.

00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.450
Meaning?

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:23.910
I mean it's safest for you to be by 
Aoi-kun's side anytime, anywhere.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.660
I figured you'd say that.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:30.930
They may be welcoming us in, but this
was enemy territory just a few days ago.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:34.920
You never know who might 
be lurking about, right?

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.850
I understand that, but...

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.280
By the way, where did Lyrule go?

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:46.860
She said she was going to help 
wash the bandages and the sheets.

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:47.800
I see.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:51.310
She's doing it as part of her training 
to control the spirits, then.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.310
What do you mean?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:55.900
Apparently, one of the basic
magic training drills

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.730
involves removing impurities
using the power of spirits.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:05.200
Oh, so that's the kind of magic that was used
to make the aroma oils used in our massages.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:08.250
According to Gale,

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:14.440
Lyrule's able to handle the spirits on par
with the emperor's elite mages.

00:21:14.440 --> 00:21:17.280
She only awakened to her magic
a month ago, right?

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:19.460
That girl's a real enigma herself.

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:22.540
Yeah. But one thing is for sure.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:28.720
She's been on our side
ever since we first came to this world.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.280
That's true.

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:33.980
The Azure Brigade folk are the ones
we can't be sure of yet.

00:21:34.390 --> 00:21:37.690
Even when they're being so welcoming?

00:21:38.060 --> 00:21:40.710
They're just hoping to appease us.

00:21:41.140 --> 00:21:44.440
They probably don't want to get into 
conflict with the Seven-Light Faith

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:47.570
while they're exhausted from 
their battle against Gustave.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:51.480
If a battle breaks out,
people will get hurt and die.

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:54.200
If we can settle things diplomatically, 
that would be for the best.

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:55.620
Tsukasa-san.

00:21:55.940 --> 00:21:59.530
Do you think we'll be able to get along
with the Azure Brigade?

00:22:03.220 --> 00:22:04.890
I'll cut right to the chase.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.340
It's impossible.
